              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "heimdall83"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Good recipe, though I wish it had more banana in it. The reviewer who said it's not a \"Passover acceptable recipe\" because it has leavening is wrong: leavening itself, even yeast, is fine, which is why wine--grapes fermented by a close cousin to bread yeast--is acceptable (as are yogurt, cheese, and pickles). There are plenty of certified brands of kosher-for-Passover baking sodas and baking powders."
